A||||4||pontiacs4me||how do I fix a pop up headlight?||||1||
Z||000000||pontiacs4me||02-26-2001||02:08 AM||||My driver side headlight wont pop up when I turn on the headlights.  I can hear the motor running when I turn on the ignition switch, and every time I turn on or turn off the headlights, but nothing happens.  What can I do to fix this?  Is it broke for good?  Can they be rebuilt and adjusted?  thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||overlord||02-26-2001||03:43 AM||||sounds like the gear inside is stripped.<BR>Mine is an 84 and i belevie you can open the motor up and flip around the gear so itll work.<P>do a search on this  topic, im sure theres plenty info.||||reg||1
Z||000002||gabriel||02-26-2001||07:08 AM||||I tried the gear flip thing - didn't work.<P>Rodney Dickman sells a complete rebuild kit that works great.<BR>       <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||02-26-2001||07:12 AM||||Quite often flipping over the gear does work since the gear traveles less than 180 degrees in its normal operation.  Be careful when you dismantle the motor so you don't let any parts spring out and forget where they go.<P>There is quite a lot written about re-building these motors that you can refer to.<P>You might start here:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html</A> <P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tweek||02-26-2001||11:54 AM||||On this subject...<P>Is it ok to disconnect that wire thats by itself running to the motor so that the headlights stay up all the time...? less wear and tear etc...<P>-Ted||||reg||1
